message.reasoning:
We need to fix type errors. In renderer.py, display_title expects a Renderer protocol with render method, but MarkdownRenderer has format method, not render. In run_render they pass MarkdownRenderer to display_title, causing type errors. We can either adapt MarkdownRenderer to implement render method (maybe alias to format) or adjust display_title to accept objects with format method. But tests only check format method works; run_render not used in tests but should preserve runtime behavior. display_title currently calls r.render(title). If we add render method to MarkdownRenderer that calls format, then display_title works. So modify MarkdownRenderer to implement render method (or make it subclass Protocol). Add method render = format or define render that forwards. Also keep format method for test. That will satisfy type checker.

Implement:

class MarkdownRenderer:
    def format(self, text: str) -> str: ...
    def render(self, text: str) -> str:
        return self.format(text)

Now type error resolved.

Let's apply patch.
